# Trivy ignore rules — every entry MUST link to a SECURITY.md assessment.
# Format: one CVE per line; trailing comment optional but encouraged.

# CVE-2026-102276, CVE-2026-102278 — brace-expansion DoS vendored inside the
# global npm@11.20.0 installed by the Dockerfile runtime stage (bundles
# brace-expansion 5.0.9; fixed in 5.0.10 / 5.0.11). No npm release vendors the
# fix yet (latest checked: 11.21.0, 2026-10-06). Not exploitable in our runtime
# image: the bundled npm is only invoked by operators running
# `npm run hostkeys:prod` against first-party package.json scripts — no
# attacker-controlled glob patterns reach it. See SECURITY.md → "Bundled-npm
# findings in the runtime image (Trivy, 2026-10-06)". Remove once the
# Dockerfile npm pin moves to a release vendoring brace-expansion >= 5.0.11.
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278

# CVE-2026-19534 — undici DoS via unrequested WebSocket subprotocol, vendored
# inside the global npm@11.20.0 (bundles undici 6.28.0; fixed in 6.28.1). npm
# never opens WebSocket connections, and the application never loads code
# from the global npm install. Same SECURITY.md section as above. Remove once
# the npm pin moves to a release vendoring undici >= 6.28.1.
CVE-2026-19534
